sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant C as CPU worker<br/>two host buffers
  participant M as MAPLE<br/>two owned queues
  participant D as DX100<br/>owned tiles and registers
  C->>M: Produce pointers for batch 0 bounds (bounded count)
  M-->>C: Submission acknowledgements (values may still be pending)
  C->>M: Consume exact counts for batch 0
  M-->>C: Begin/end values associated with batch 0 vertices
  loop Each admitted current batch n
    opt A following batch exists
      C->>M: Submit batch n+1 into now-empty queues
      M-->>C: Submission acknowledgements
    end
    Note over M,D: MAPLE may fetch n+1<br/>while DX100 and CPU work on n
    C->>D: Stage n's row bounds<br/>publish counts and visibility<br/>initialize register values
    loop All neighbor chunks, including long-row continuation
      C->>D: Expand ranges and gather neighbors
      C->>D: Wait for usable associated outputs
      D-->>C: Row ordinals and neighbor IDs
      Note right of C: CPU parent read / CAS<br/>retained store / queue push
      C->>D: Cover consumers before chunk tile reuse
    end
    C->>D: Confirm exhaustion and finish batch consumers
    opt A following batch exists
      C->>M: Consume n+1's exact result counts
      M-->>C: Bounds for next current batch
      Note right of C: Exchange metadata buffers
    end
  end
  C->>M: Establish known-count completion and deployment quiescence
  C->>D: Establish final consumer completion and safe release
  Note right of C: Flush and join workers<br/>publish next frontier
